# Audit review rules

Context: authorized review of the owner's own apps.
Repos: `shahafrach/haimunia-club` (Haimunia club, live at https://haimunia.pages.dev) and `shahafrach/haimunia-app-demo` (BOX-LOG and the shared Supabase backend, project box-log). Old club app, read only: `haimuniya/haimunia-app`.

## Branch and production safety

- Work on a new branch `audit/<task-id>`. Never push to `main`.
- Never change production data or settings.
- Run tests and data checks only against the local stack (`supabase start`) and the test accounts in `~/dev/audit.env`.

## Findings only — do not fix app code

- Do not fix app code during review tasks.
- Record each issue in `FINDINGS.md` with: ID, severity (`critical` / `high` / `medium` / `low`), app, file or URL, steps to reproduce, expected vs actual, suggested fix, `status=open`.

## Test discipline

- Run only the tests related to the current step.
- One full run at the end, in the foreground.
- No background watchers, sleep loops or polling.
- Do not re-run a suite that passed.

## End of task report

End with a short English report: what you checked, counts by severity, top 3 issues, what you could not check and why.
